  "statement": {
    "case_for": "B051 recognizes an original instrument-level advance that opened direct and quantitative access to atomic-scale structure. Aberration correction overcame a fundamental electron-optical limitation; its widespread, durable use and transformative consequences for imaging and chemical analysis provide unusually strong experimental verification. Rose supplies the essential corrector concepts, while Haider and Urban represent the crucial practical realization and demonstration.",
    "case_against": "The achievement arose through several correction schemes, instrument-development teams, and later engineering advances. Before a final decision, the historical record must establish whether this trio fairly captures the original theory-to-working-instrument chain without excluding comparably indispensable contributors.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "kroll-stefan",
        "point": "Kroll regards B051 as transformative but argues that parallel correction schemes and industrial development complicate exclusive attribution.",
        "response": "I agree that this is the central reservation and would not treat routine modern performance as evidence of priority by itself. Nonetheless, the proposed three names identify a coherent chain from decisive optical concepts to practical corrected microscopes; archival attribution review can test that chain directly."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "eriksson-olle",
        "point": "Eriksson emphasizes that aberration correction made direct sub-angstrom imaging and chemically resolved materials science routine, while also calling for scrutiny of the relative credit among developers.",
        "response": "This is the appropriate experimental standard: the advance is not merely an elegant design but a repeatedly demonstrated capability that changed what can be seen. I retain B051 as preferred, while treating the exact division among Rose, Haider, and Urban as a necessary historical question rather than a settled inference."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "johansson-goran",
        "point": "Johansson favors B003 because optical lattice clocks combine a clear original principle, decisive experimental realization, and exceptional reproducibility.",
        "response": "B003 is an excellent alternative with compact attribution to Katori and Ye. I give B051 priority because its experimental door-opening effect is already embedded across materials physics, but the clock case may prove cleaner if the microscopy attribution cannot be resolved convincingly."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether Harald Rose, Maximilian Haider, and Knut Urban are the uniquely appropriate limited attribution among parallel corrector concepts, implementations, and industrial teams.",
